and performing it, given that the simulation will agree with the
experiment within some epsilon? If I can replace the meat with
silicon, why can't I replace the silicon with a simulation of its
behavior (engineers build microchips all the time by simulating 
silicon and it seems to work) It seems you are postulating a behavior
of matter which we don't normally observe. You could claim that when
matter couples to the "consciousness ghost", it acts differently,
but then, I'd expect biologists to have encountered this phenomena already.

> Let's say when I experience "green" a particular neuronal structure is
