   What you've done is map the Chinese room into an isomorphically
identical situation. Now the question is, how far can you reduce
a neuronal structure before reductionism fails and your "hardware
dependency" kicks in? You've reduced the problem of simulating
the brain to the problem of simulating neurons. My response is,
why can't we simulate neurons? (in fact, I don't need to answer the
